Z||000000||fropuff||04-03-2001||08:26 PM||||Hey paint guys!  (and all you intruders;  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  That's okay.  You guys can answer too!)  I have a question.  I need a new front fascia for my GT, and I have a source for one, but it will needed painted.  When this is being done, I also want to get the ground FX painted.  I was wondering...what would you guys charge to paint the fascia red, and the ground FX gray?  I would take off the ground FX, and wet sand all parts.  The only masking would be on the rear fascia, and the front fascia after the red it sprayed on.  So, what would you guys charge to shoot it?  I want to know what to expect.  Thanks a lot.<P>*I mean by a guy in his garage booth, not a professional company.  Thanks again!!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||04-04-2001||10:32 PM||||your going to need a pint of each color, from $25-$45 each, reducer for both. Then your going to need the clear topcoat, $30 qt and hardner at about another $30. Then tape and masking paper. so figure $150 or so for material. labor is whatever he'll take. If you just sanded it for me, prob be about $200 labor shop price.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||04-12-2001||05:57 PM||||Okay, I just found some red base coat that we used to paint the car last summer.  There's around a pint of it there, so I'm fine for that.  It'll also match the rest of the car.  All I need is the silver base, clear top coat, reducer, tape and sand paper.  What would you guys charge if I both wetsanded and masked the panels?  Around $200 isn't too bad, considering I'm getting a good deal on the fascia.  Would you rather paint the ground effects on the car or off?  Okay, that about does it.  Thanks for the help!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
